Here is the commit message:
fixed /help bug

Here is the root cause:
In `AbstractCommand`, the constructor used the full `name` string (which may include argument placeholders, e.g. "kick <player>") to build the initial `helpText`, but then truncated `name` to only the first token for internal use (command lookup). The `reloadText()` method (used to refresh the cached `helpText`, e.g. after a language/config reload) incorrectly rebuilt `helpText` using this already-truncated `name` field instead of the original full name. This caused any command with arguments to lose its argument description in `/help` output once `reload()` was triggered (e.g. after `/reload` or on server reconfiguration). The subclasses `PlayerArgCommand`, `OnlinePlayerArgCommand`, and `InvalidCommand` duplicated this same flawed caching/reload pattern, compounding the problem, and required `CommandParser`/`Server` to explicitly invoke `reload()` to keep help text in sync — an inherently fragile design that the patch replaces with a stateless, on-demand `getHelpText()` computed directly from an immutable original name field.

